# Trivy CVE allowlist for nginx-geoip.
#
# All entries are time-boxed via `exp:` — Trivy will resume reporting them
# after the expiration date so they cannot rot silently. Bump the dates
# only after re-confirming the analysis below.
#
# Review cadence: every entry has a one-month expiry from the day it was
# added. On expiry, either:
#   1. supercronic has been rebuilt with a patched Go toolchain — remove
#      the entry entirely, or
#   2. the analysis still holds — extend the expiry by another month and
#      note the new check date in the comment.

# ─── Go stdlib in usr/local/bin/supercronic ────────────────────────────────
# supercronic v0.2.45 (latest, released 2026-04-23) is built with Go 1.26.2.
# Five HIGH CVEs in Go's stdlib were fixed in Go 1.25.10 / 1.26.3 but
# aptible/supercronic has not yet shipped a rebuild. The renovate manager
# (Dockerfile line ~52: `# renovate: datasource=github-releases
# depName=aptible/supercronic`) will pick up the next release automatically;
# at that point this entire block becomes obsolete.
#
# Reachability analysis (per CVE) is documented inline. supercronic in this
# image is invoked as `supercronic -quiet -passthrough-logs /tmp/nginx-crontab`
# — no `-prometheus-listen-address`, no `-debug`, no `-test` at runtime — so
# the only attack surface is reading the crontab file (which we generate
# ourselves, not user input) and forking the cron-defined commands.

# CVE-2026-33811: net/cgo LookupCNAME — very long CNAME crashes the cgo
# resolver. supercronic does not perform user-driven DNS lookups; it only
# exec()s the cron commands listed in /tmp/nginx-crontab (geoip-cron.sh,
# uptimerobot-cron.sh, logrotate-cron.sh). Not reachable.
CVE-2026-33811 exp:2026-06-19

# CVE-2026-33814: net/http2 SETTINGS-frame infinite loop in the transport.
# supercronic exposes no HTTP server here (no -prometheus-listen-address)
# and does not act as an HTTP client. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-33814 exp:2026-06-19

# CVE-2026-39820: net/mail.ParseAddress / ParseAddressList malformed-input
# handling. supercronic does not parse email addresses. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-39820 exp:2026-06-19

# CVE-2026-39836: net.Dial / LookupPort NUL-byte panic — Windows-only code
# path. We run linux/amd64 and linux/arm64. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-39836 exp:2026-06-19

# CVE-2026-42499: net/mail consumePhrase DoS. Same surface as CVE-2026-39820
# — supercronic does not parse mail phrases. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-42499 exp:2026-06-19
